Problem: Given an array arr[], determine if it can be partitioned into two subsets such that the sum of elements in both parts is the same.

Note: Each element must be in exactly one subset.   


#Approach: 
#* As we know the , we need to divide array in two equal sum part, so total sum of array should be even number, because odd number can't divide in two part.
#* we use knapsack 0/1 approach , need to add array arr[i] value in sum1 or sum2 means take or leave that value.
#* if we reach at length of array , then we have to check whether sum1==sum2, meanse subset1 sum equal to subset2 sum
#* also used dp as if given index , sum1 and sum2 value already calculated , we don't need to calculate again

class Solution:
    def equalPartition(self, arr):
        if sum(arr)%2!=0 or len(arr)==1:
            return False
        dp={}
        return self.myfun(arr,0,0,0,dp)
    def myfun(self,arr,sum1,sum2,ind,dp):
        #we will go from 0 to n
        if ind==len(arr):
            return sum1==sum2
        if (ind,sum1,sum2) in dp:
            return dp[(ind,sum1,sum2)]
        take = self.myfun(arr,sum1+arr[ind],sum2,ind+1,dp)
        leave= self.myfun(arr,sum1,sum2+arr[ind],ind+1,dp)
        dp[(ind,sum1,sum2)]= take or leave
        return dp[(ind,sum1,sum2)]
